      "content": "The marginal tax rate myth: only dollars ABOVE the bracket threshold are taxed at the higher rate —\n\nThe marginal tax rate myth: only dollars ABOVE the bracket threshold are taxed at the higher rate — not all income. Single filer earning $100K pays ~18% effective federal rate, not 24% marginal. You cannot earn your way into lower take-home pay by crossing a bracket. #moneyfacts #taxes #taxbracket #marginalrate #financialliteracy",
